Apple Inc. (AAPL) has filed new documents (https://apps.fcc.gov/eas/GetApplicationAttachment.html?id=3719077) with the Federal Communications Commission that suggest its HomePod speaker launch may be approaching. Made public Friday, the documents include a diagram of the bottom of a "wireless speaker" that includes the location of an FCC label required on such devices and a series of reports about the radio emissions dated Nov. 8, 2017. Apple stock is up a fraction to $178.56 in late trading. Already a late entrant, behind tech titans such as (http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-booming-smart-speaker-market-and-the-services-it-will-help-2018-01-18) Amazon.com Inc. (AMZN) and Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL) [s:goog], Apple delayed its smart speaker launch in November (http://www.marketwatch.com/story/apple-delays-homepod-smart-speaker-for-unknown-reasons-2017-11-17), and said it would ship in early 2018. Apple stock is up 49% in the last 12 months, as the S&P 500 index has gained 24%. The Dow Jones Industrial Average , of which Apple is a component, gained 32% in the past 12 months.
-Max A. Cherney;
 19-18 1729ET
